ngale problems in quantitative finance.</p>\n<p><a href=\"../../resources/mit18_642_f24_lec19_1_pdf/index.html\">Stochastic Calculus Slides (PDF)</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"../../resources/mit18_642_f24_lec19_2_pdf/index.html\">Simulations of Brownian Motion (PDF)</a></p>\n\n    <h3 id=\"lecture-25\">Lecture 25</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"video-embed video-player-wrapper\">\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  <div class=\"show-offline alert alert-warning\" role=\"alert\">\n    \n    \n      <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"24\">\n  <path d=\"M0 0h24v24H0z\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <path d=\"M15.5 14h-.79l-.28-.27C15.41 12.59 16 11.11 16 9.5 16 5.91 13.09 3 9.5 3S3 5.91 3 9.5 5.91 16 9.5 16c1.61 0 3.09-.59 4.23-1.57l.27.28v.79l5 4.99L20.49 19l-4.99-5zm-6 0C7.01 14 5 11.99 5 9.5S7.01 5 9.5 5 14 7.01 14 9.5 11.99 14 9.5 14z\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n</svg>\n\n    \n    Viewing videos requires an internet connection\n  </div>\n\n<div class=\"video-container embedded-video-container youtube-container\">\n  <video\n    id=\"video-player-H4V29wkHYb4-ef1af49d9683c9255ca90fcfca093441\"\n    class=\"video-js vjs-default-skin vjs-big-play-centered vjs-ocw\"\n    controls\n    data-downloadlink = \"../../static_resources/18642-lecture-25-version-2_360p_16_9.mp4\"\n    data-transcriptlink = \"\"\n    \n  >\n      \n  </video>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<script>\n  window.handleVideoJSError = function(err) {\n    console.error('Error loading VideoJS or YouTube player:', err)\n    var youtubeVideoContainers = document.querySelectorAll('.video-container.youtube-container')\n    for (var i = 0; i < youtubeVideoContainers.length; i++) {\n      youtubeVideoContainers[i].style.display = 'none';\n    }\n\n    var fallbackContainers = document.querySelectorAll('.video-fallback-container')\n    for (var j = 0; j < fallbackContainers.length; j++) {\n      fallbackContainers[j].style.display = 'block';\n    }\n  }\n\n  try {\n      new Function(\"class X{#abc;}; 1??2; ({})?.abc\");\n  }\n  catch (e) {\n    window.handleVideoJSError(e)\n  }\n\n  window.addEventListener('load', function() {\n    if (window.initVideoJS) {\n      window.initVideoJS()\n    }\n  })\n</script>\n\n\n\n  \n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"video-tab-toggle-section pointer\">\n  <div class=\"video-tab-header d-flex\">\n    \n      <span class=\"tab-title-section\">\n        \n          <a href=\"../../resources/18642-lecture-25-version-2_mp4/index.html\" aria-label=\"View video page\">\n          <i class=\"material-icons toggle md-18\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>\n<span class=\"tab-title\">View video page</span>\n\n          </a>\n        \n      </span>\n    \n    \n    \n      <div class=\"ml-auto\">\n        <button class=\"video-download-icons\" aria-label=\"Show Downloads\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n          <img class=\"video-download-icon\" src=\"/static_shared/images/videojs_download.e0dbb2cfb52d2d71ba4a.svg\" aria-hidden=\"true\"/>\n          <i class=\"material-icons caret-down\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>\n        </button>\n      </div>\n    \n  </div>\n  \n  <div class=\"video-tab-download-popup hidden\">\n    \n    <div class=\"download-menu-main\">\n      <ul>\n        \n          <li>\n            <a href=\"../../static_resources/18642-lecture-25-version-2_360p_16_9.mp4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" aria-label=\"Download video\" download>Download video</a>\n          </li>\n        \n        \n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    \n    \n  </div>\n  \n</div>\n\n<div class=\"video-tab container collapse pr-0 \" role=\"tabpanel\">\n  <div class=\"video-tab-content-section\">\n    \n  </div>\n</div>\n\n  \n</div>\n\n<p><strong>Video description:</strong> This final lecture provides an in-depth discussion of Itô’s formula and its generalizations, illustrating how it applies to functions of Brownian motion, especially in finance for modeling derivative pricing and geometric Brownian motion. It also explains the derivation of the Black-Scholes differential equation through risk-neutral hedging, the solution of the heat (diffusion) equation as a fundamental tool for solving such PDEs, and introduces more advanced stochastic differential equations like the Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process, emphasizing their broad applications beyond finance.</p>\n<p><a href=\"../../resources/mit18_642_f24_lec24_pdf/index.html\">Stochastic Differential Equations Slides (PDF)</a></p>\n",
